  "id": "Compound::DB00307 - Disease::DOID:2531",
  "verbalization": "Bexarotene is linked to Hematologic Cancer through multiple pathways that converge on its role in treating this condition. The evidence suggests that Bexarotene, as a member of the Retinoid family, interacts with Retinoic Acid Agents, which are known to influence cellular differentiation and proliferation. This mechanism is further supported by its association with Alitretinoin, a Retinoid that directly targets Hematologic Cancer. Additionally, Bexarotene's ability to cause Hypolipidaemia and its relationship with Antineoplastic Agents, such as Doxorubicin and Epirubicin, which also treat Hematologic Cancer, highlights a broader pharmacological profile that may contribute to its therapeutic effects.\n\nThe integration of these pathways underscores the importance of Retinoids in modulating cellular processes that are dysregulated in hematologic malignancies. While the exact mechanism by which Retinoids exert their anti-cancer effects remains under investigation, the shared pathways and ontological connections suggest a potential role in regulating cell cycle progression, apoptosis, and tumor growth. The evidence also indicates that Bexarotene may act through multiple mechanisms, including both direct and indirect pathways, which could explain its efficacy in treating hematologic cancers.",
